window.KB_BODY[42]={"tsb102237":"<h2>Revision, Multiple Steps, Fuel Filter Head Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 006-017 (Fuel Filter Head) in Section 1. Changes include instructions for the removal and installation of filter spuds and a leak check in the Finishing Step.</p>","tsb102250":"<h2>Revision, Install Step, Straight Thread Plug Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 017-011 (Straight Thread Plug) in Section 17. The torque specifications for metric straight thread o-rings plugs used on QSK45 and QSK60 engines have been included.</p>","tsb102253":"<h2>Revision, Measure Step, Cylinder Block Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates Procedure 001-026, Cylinder Block, to show the correct minimum value for the lower counterbore inside diameter (Lower Press Fit).</p>","tsb102254":"<h2>Revision, Test Step, Engine Run In (Engine Dynamometer) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates Procedure 014-006, Engine Run In (Engine Dynamometer), to remove a reference to a service tool that is not available through QuickServe Online.</p>","tsb102282":"<h2>Revision, Measure Step, Fuel Inlet Restriction Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the measure step in Procedure 006-020 (Fuel Inlet Restriction) in Section 6 of the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p>","tsb102325":"<h2>Revision, Measure Step, Cylinder Block Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the main bearing bore diameter dimensions in the Measure Step of Procedure 001-026, Cylinder Block.</p>","tsb102339":"<h2>Revision, Initial Check Step, Injector Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 006-026 (Injector) in Section 6 of the Service Manual, QSK45 and QSK60, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. The procedure is being revised to add information on how to determine if the high-pressure injection (HPI) injectors have run dry (without fuel) and to check the engine.</p>","tsb102346":"<h2>Revision, Assembly Step, Cylinder Head Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announcs a new drop gauge, Part Number 4918779. The drop gauge is used to measure valve guide straightness and diameter after pressing the valve guide into the cylinder head during cylinder head rebuild on the QSK45 and QSK60 engines.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102347":"<h2>Addition, Service Tool Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds the Drop Gauge service tool for checking the valve guides, to the Service Tool Procedure 022-001_02 in Section 22.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102366":"<h2>Revision, Troubleshooting Overview Procedure and Coolant Loss Symptom Tree</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Troubleshooting Overview Procedure t00-004 in Section TS and the Coolant Loss symptom tree.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102367":"<h2>Addition, Pressure Test Step, Cooling System Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds the Pressure Test step to the Cooling System Procedure 008-018 in Section 8.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102368":"<h2>Addition, Service Tool Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds service tools Fluorescent Tracer Dye and Black Light Lamp Kit to the Service Tools Procedure 022-001_08 in Section 8.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102387":"<h2>Addition, Multiple Steps, Crankshaft Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds the QSKV counter weight torque to the Clean and Inspect for Reuse step in the Crankshaft Procedure 001-016 in Section 1.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102388":"<h2>Revision, Install Step, Idler Gear, Camshaft (Right Bank) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to correct the positioning of the oil hole when assembling the right bank camshaft idler shaft on the QSK45 and QSK60 engine, <a class=\"lnk doc\" href=\"#/doc/56-001-038-tr\">Procedure 001-038 (Idler Gear, Camshaft (Right Bank)) in Section 1.</a></p>","tsb102400":"<h2>Revision, General Information, Overhead Set (OBC) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic intends to make it clear that QSK45 and QSK60 engines with the Quantum fuel system (mechanically actuated injectors) no longer require a valve and injector set to be performed at 1500 hours. Instead, the valves and injectors will <b>only</b> be adjusted when the injector is serviced.</p><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the General Information step of Procedure 003-006 (Overhead Set (OBC)) to include a statement that reflects the guidelines for adjusting the overhead.</p>","tsb102401":"<h2>Revision, Maintenance Schedule</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic intends to make it clear that QSK45 and QSK60 engines with the Quantum fuel system (mechanically actuated injectors) no longer require a valve and injector set to be performed at 1500 hours. Instead, the valves and injectors will <b>only</b> be adjusted when the injector is serviced.</p><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the maintenance schedule, Procedure 102-002 (Maintenance Schedule) to remove the scheduled item for adjusting the overhead.</p>","tsb102438":"<h2>Revision, Measure Step, Cylinder Block Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service Parts Topic revises the part numbers shown in the Measure Step of Procedure 001-056, Cylinder Block.</p>","tsb102445":"<h2>Revision to Troubleshooting Trees t022, t023, t024, and t096</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the following troubleshooting trees for the QSK45 and QSK60 engines:</p><ul><li><a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>-t022 - Coolant Temperature Above Normal - Gradual Overheat</li><li><a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>-t023 - Coolant Temperature Above Normal - Sudden Overheat</li><li><a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>-t024 - Coolant Temperature Below Normal</li><li><a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>-t096 - Intake Manifold Air Temperature Above Specification.</li></ul><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102457":"<h2>Revision, Symptom Tree t027, Crankcase Gases (Blowby) Excessive</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises symptom tree t027, Crankcase Gases (Blowby) Excessive.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102460":"<h2>Revision, Clean and Inspect for Reuse, Cylinder Liner Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to revise the Clean and Inspect for Reuse steps for Procedure 001-028 (Cylinder Liner).</p>","tsb102484":"<h2>Revision, Inspect Step, Lubricating Oil Filter (Spin-On) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises 007-013 (Lubricating Oil Filter (Spin-On)) the Inspect step to include aftercooler fretting as a possible location for aluminum in the oil.</p>","tsb102500":"<h2>Addition, Single and Double Nut Configuration Rebuild Instructions, (Fan Hub, Belt Driven) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds single nut (406 mm [15.98 in] diameter hub) and double nut (450 mm [17.72 in] diameter hub) configuration rebuild instructions to Procedure 008-036 (Fan Hub, Belt Driven).</p>","tsb102506":"<h2>Revision, Measure Step, Cylinder Block and Liner Seats Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-027 (Cylinder Block and Liner Seats) in Section 1 of the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. Oversize liners have been included.</p>","tsb102510":"<h2>Complete Revision, Sensor Wiring Harness Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds the content from Procedures 019-043 (Engine Wiring Harness) to 019-081 (Sensor Wiring Harness). In addition, wiring harness bracket and cover torques have been included. Procedure 019-043 (Engine Wiring Harness) is no longer included in the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, CENSE™ System, QSK45 and QSK60 Engine Series, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666410\">3666410</a>.</p>","tsb102513":"<h2>Revision, Install Step, Injector Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the torque value of the mechanically actuated injector hold-down capscrew in Procedure 006-026 (Injector). The new torque value for the injector hold-down capscrew is 75 N•m [55 ft-lb].</p>","tsb102530":"<h2>Revision, Preparatory Step, Engine Run-in (Without Dynamometer) Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to revise the Preparatory Step for Procedure 014-004, Engine Run-in (Without Dynamometer). The requirements to pre heat the engine and the use of SAE 10W-30 lubricating oil has been removed.</p>","tsb102547":"<h2>Revision, Remove Step, Piston Cooling Nozzle Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to revise the Remove step in Procedure 001-046 (Piston Cooling Nozzle). This allows the field to reuse the piston cooling nozzles, providing they are handled with care and inspected before they are placed back into the engine.</p>","tsb102556":"<h2>Revision, Multiple Steps, Maintenance Schedule Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the maintenance schedule by removing the reference in the schedule to &#x27;see Section V for oil replacement based on analysis&#x27; statement and replacing the statement with a reference to the Cummins® Engine Oil and Oil Analysis Recommendations, Bulletin 3810340. Multiple revisions to the Oil Drain Interval step have been made also.</p>","tsb102557":"<h2>Revision, Assembly Step, Fan Drive Idler Arm Assembly Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is revise the assembly step in Procedure 008-029 (Fan Drive Idler Arm Assembly) in Group 8. The procedure now includes a slide arm design idler assembly.</p>","tsb102618":"<h2>Revision, Torque Value, (Bearings, Main) and Crankshaft Procedures</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the torque specification for main bearing side bolts in Procedures 001-006 (Bearings, Main) and 001-016 (Crankshaft) in Section 1.</p>","tsb102657":"<h2>Complete Replacement, Cylinder Block Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic releases common Procedure 001-026 (Cylinder Block) for the QSK45, QSK60, QSK45G, and QSK60G engines.</p>","tsb102666":"<h2>New Procedure, Piston and Cylinder Liner</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces new Procedure 001-045 (Piston and Cylinder Liner) to the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p><p>The procedure includes the removal and installation steps required for the new straight split connecting rod used in QSK45 and QSK60 engines. The cylinder liner, piston and connecting rod <b>must</b> be removed as a complete assembly.</p>","tsb102668":"<h2>Revision, Remove Step, Crankshaft Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Remove Step in Procedure 001-016 (Crankshaft) in Section 1, of the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. The Main Bearing Cap Puller service tool number has been revised.</p>","tsb102697":"<h2>Revision, Multiple Steps, Connecting Rod Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>The purpose of the Service/Parts Topic is to add a General Information section, revise the Clean and Inspect for Reuse section, and revise the Measure section in the Connecting Rod procedure (001-014).</p>","tsb102719":"<h2>Revision, Multiple Sections, Piston Cooling Nozzle Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises multiple sections of Procedure 001-046 (Piston Cooling Nozzle). There are now two types of piston cooling nozzles available for QSK45 and QSK60 engines. This procedure has been updated to include information to distinguish between the two nozzle types.</p>","tsb102720":"<h2>Revision, Install Section, Crosshead Procedure and Revision, Clean and Inspect for Reuse Section, Cylinder Head Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts topic revises two procedures in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual:</p><p>002-001 (Crosshead) in Section 2, the Install section, valve stem tip check has been added.</p><p>002-004 (Cylinder Head) in Section 2, the Inspect for Reuse section, valve stem tip check has been added.</p>","tsb102728":"<h2>Release of (Gear Housing, Front) and Cylinder Block Liner Bore Concentricity Procedures</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic releases Procedure 84-001-033 (Gear Housing, Front) for the QSK45G and QSK60G engines and common Procedure 102-001-070 (Cylinder Block Liner Bore Concentricity) for the QSK45, QSK60, QSK45G, and QSK60G engines.</p>","tsb102744":"<h2>Revision, Specifications, Lubricating Oil System</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts topic revises the specifications for the Lubricating Oil System, sump configuration and capacities.</p>","tsb102804":"<h2>Revision, General Information, Procedure 002-004 (Cylinder Head)</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a new stamping code that indicates the size of the valve guide seal for all K and QSK ReCon® cylinder heads. The stamping code was implemented on 5 February 2008.</p>","tsb102836":"<h2>Engine Run-in (Without Dynamometer) Procedure, Preparatory Steps Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic supersedes 07T14-1. Replace 07T14-1 with this topic. Two notes were taken out of the Preparatory Step that no londer apply to the procedure.</p>","tsb102851":"<h2>Addition, Measurement for Oversize Head Gasket for Cylinder Block and Liner Seats Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds measurement specifications for oversize head gaskets to the Clean and Inspect for Reuse step in Procedure 001-027 (Cylinder Block and Liner Seats).</p>","tsb102853":"<h2>Low-Temperature Aftercooler Water (LTA) Pump Procedure, Oil Feed Hose Information Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Remove and Install sections of Procedure 008-109 (Low-Temperature Aftercooler (LTA) Water Pump). Instructions for the oil feed hose has been included.</p>","tsb102854":"<h2>Lubricating Oil Pump Procedure, Clean and Inspect for Reuse Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Clean and Inspect for Reuse section of Procedure 007-031 (Lubricating Oil Pump). The pressure regulator spring specifications were revised.</p>","tsb102897":"<h2>(Fan Hub, Belt Driven) Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revised Procedure 008-036 (Fan Hub, Belt Driven) in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>, with the removal of the K38 and K50 manual sections from this procedure.</p>","tsb102902":"<h2>Crankshaft Seals, RTV on Outer Diameter</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic supercedes topic 06T1-28. Replace 06T1-28 with this topic.</p><p>This Service/Parts Topic updates Procedure 001-023 (Front Crankshaft Seal) and Procedure 001-024 (Rear Crankshaft Seal).</p><p>When the front or rear crankshaft seals are installed, it is necessary to apply a small bead of high performance RTV sealant Part Number 4918771 (Loctite™5920) or equivalent to the outside diameter of the seal. The purpose of the RTV is to reduce the possibility of oil leaks between the seal and the mounting plate. The engine serial number first with this seal configuration is 331157377, built 04 August 2004.</p><p>Crankshaft Seals requiring high performance RTV sealant Part Number 4918771 (Loctite™5920) or equivalent:</p><ul><li>Front crankshaft seal, Part Number 4100624</li><li>Rear crankshaft seal, Part Number 4100625</li></ul><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102921":"<h2>Camshaft Procedure, Remove Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds a table, Camshaft Guide Installation Chart, to the Remove Section of the Camshaft procedure to show the correct c-clip positions for the camshaft removal tool.</p>","tsb102936":"<h2>Revision, Cylinder Liner Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-028 (Cylinder Liner) in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. The Remove step has been revised to change the recommended cylinder liner removal service tool to Part Number 3163745.</p>","tsb102948":"<h2>Additional Inspection Steps, Two Procedures and One Symptom Tree</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Troubleshooting Symptom Tree t105 (Lubricating Oil Pressure Low) in Section TS, Procedure 007-013 (Lubricating Oil Filter (Spin-On)) and Procedure 007-067 (Eliminator Filter) in Section 7 of the Service Manual, QSK45 and QSK60, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. A change was made to inspect the lubricating pump idler shaft and gear in the Inspect section if debris is found.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb102986":"<h2>Fleetguard™ Centrifuge Procedure, Assemble Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Assemble section in Procedure 007-068 (Fleetguard™ Centrifuge) to include a new illustration and additional instructions to be used in the assembly process.</p>","tsb103097":"<h2>Piston and Connecting Rod Assembly Procedure, Remove Section Revision; Connecting Rod Procedure, Measure Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedures 001-054 (Piston and Connecting Rod Assembly) and 001-014 (Connecting Rod) in Section 1 of the Service Manual, QSK45 and QSK60, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p><p>The piston and connecting rod assembly procedure was revised for split angle split connecting rods <b>only</b> and the connecting rod procedure torque values were revised.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb103098":"<h2>Fuel Manifold (Supply) Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises multiple sections in Procedure 006-022 (Fuel Manifold (Supply)) in Section 6 of the QSK 45 and QSK 60 Series Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p>","tsb103129":"<h2>Piston and Cylinder Liner Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-045 (Piston and Cylinder Liner) in Section 1 of the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p><p>An additional cylinder liner removal tool and related usage has been added, in addition to the inclusion of a straight torque value for tightening the connecting rods when working through the hand hole covers.</p>","tsb103132":"<h2>Piston Procedure, Clean and Inspect for Reuse Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-043 (Piston) in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. The revision includes new minimum reuse limits for the top piston ring groove in the Ring Groove Wear Limits table. The top ring groove wear limits have been modified to a minimum specification of 159.10 mm [6.264 in].</p>","tsb103209":"<h2>Eliminator™ Filter Procedure, Assemble Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces a revision to the Assemble Section of Procedure 007-067 (Eliminator™ Filter). The hydraulic motor mounting capscrew torque value has been revised.</p>","tsb103220":"<h2>Fan Drive Idler Arm Assembly Procedure, Assembly Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is revise the assembly section in Procedure 008-029 (Fan Drive Idler Arm Assembly). The assembly torque specifications in the summary now match the specifications in the step.</p>","tsb103221":"<h2>Pre-Lubricating Oil Pump Procedure, Install Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the mounting bracket capscrew torque value in the Install section of Procedure 007-063 (Pre-Lubricating Oil Pump).</p>","tsb103222":"<h2>Aftercooler Assembly Procedure, Assemble Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic announces revisions to the Assemble section of Procedure 010-002 (Aftercooler Assembly).</p><p>The revisions clarify the Assemble section of the procedure by removing information about the installation of the lower cooler element gasket.</p><p>Only one gasket is used; between the aftercooler support and aftercooler cover.</p>","tsb103265":"<h2>Multiple Group 01 Procedure Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic documents revisions to Procedures 001-026 (Cylinder Block), 001-037 (Idler Gear, Camshaft (Left Bank)), 001-038 (Idler Gear, Camshaft (Right Bank)), 001-039 (Idler Gear, Hydraulic Pump), and 001-040 (Idler Gear, Water Pump). The revisions include specifications changes in the Clean and Inspect for Reuse section.</p>","tsb103271":"<h2>Fuel Drain Lines Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic documents the addition of the removal and installation process for the new style fuel drain line bracket to the Remove and Install sections of Procedure 006-013 (Fuel Drain Lines).</p>","tsb103273":"<h2>Air Leaks, Compressed Air System Procedure Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to revise Procedure 012-019 (Air Leaks, Compressed Air System) in order to include this procedure in Section 4 of the Operation and Maintenance Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666260\">3666260</a>. This procedure needs to be performed for all compressed air systems to prevent carbon build-up and possible failure of the compressed air system.</p>","tsb103274":"<h2>(Air Leaks, Compressed Air System) Procedure Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This purpose of this Service/Parts Topic is to revise the Maintenance Schedule in order to include Procedure 012-019 (Air Leaks, Compressed Air System) into Section 4 of the Operation and Maintenance Manual QSK45 and QSK60 Series Engines, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/3666260\">3666260</a>, so that it is checked on a regular basis. This procedure needs to be performed for all compressed air systems to prevent carbon build-up and possible failure of the compressed air system.</p>","tsb103289":"<h2>Gear Cover Trunion Sleeve, New Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a new Procedure 001-030 (Gear Cover Trunion Sleeve) in Section 1, in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p>","tsb103306":"<h2>Fuel Pump Procedure, Multple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 005-016 in Section 5 to include information about painting the fuel pump after it is installed.</p>","tsb103307":"<h2>Injector Procedure, Multple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 006-026 (Injector) in Section 6 to includ information about painting the exposed portion of the electronically actuated injector to prevent the formation of rust and corrosion.</p>","tsb103354":"<h2>Camshaft Bushings Procedure, Major Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises multiple sections of Procedure 001-010 (Camshaft Bushings).</p>","tsb103361":"<h2>(Exhaust Manifold, Dry) Procedure, Install Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Install Section of Procedure 011-007 (Exhaust Manifold, Dry) in the Service Manual, QSK45 and QSK60, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. The installation of the lockplates has been revised.</p>","tsb103392":"<h2>Cylinder Head Procedure, Clean and Inspect for Reuse Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds a step to the Clean and Inspect for Reuse section of Procedure 002-004 (Cylinder Head). A check for cracked exhaust port divider has been added.</p>","tsb103400":"<h2>Cylinder Head Procedure, Assemble Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises procedure 002-004 (Cylinder Head) for the QSK45 and QSK60 CM850 MCRS engines. The instruction to repair the cylinder head injector seats, if found out of specification, has been removed from the Assemble section for mechanical and electronically actuated injectors.</p>","tsb103401":"<h2>(Bearings, Main) Procedure, Remove Section Revision and Crankshaft Procedure, Multiple Section Additions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises procedures 001-006 (Bearings, Main) and 001-016 (Crankshaft) for the QSK45 and QSK60 engines.</p><p>The Remove section has been revised for procedure 001-006 in Section 1. Preparatory and Finishing sections have been added to procedure 001-016 in Section 1.</p>","tsb103420":"<h2>Cylinder Block and Liner Seats Procedure, Major Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises multiple sections of Procedure 001-027 (Cylinder Block and Liner Seats).</p>","tsb103421":"<h2>Cylinder Block Procedure, Major Revision, and Removal of Cylinder Liner Bore Concentricity Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a complete revision of Procedure 001-026 (Cylinder Block) and removes Procedure 001-070 (Cylinder Liner Bore Concentricity).</p>","tsb103435":"<h2>Aftercooler Assembly Procedure, Install Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the hose clamp torque in the Install section of Procedure 010-002 (Aftercooler Assembly).</p>","tsb103497":"<h2>Flywheel Housing Procedure, Install Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds a torque value for the rear engine mounts in the Install section of Procedure 016-006 (Flywheel Housing) in Section 16.</p>","tsb103512":"<h2>Coolant Thermostat Procedure, Install Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the installation torque value for the new QSK60 thermostat clamping plates and cover plates. This is the same thermostat housing used on the QSK60 with electronically actuated injectors.</p>","tsb103513":"<h2>Turbocharger Procedure, V-Band Clamp Torque Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the torque value for the V-band clamp on the HX02 turbocharger in the Assemble section of Procedure 010-033 (Turbocharger) in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p>","tsb103804":"<h2>Cylinder Block and Liner Seats Procedure, Measure Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Measure section of Procedure 001-027 (Cylinder Block and Liner Seats) for Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. The minimum specification for the Counterbore Diameter - Lower Press Fit Diameter has been changed from a specification of 181.47 mm [7.144 in] to a new specification of 181.74 mm [7.155 in].</p>","tsb103819":"<h2>Cylinder Block Procedure, Head Deck Surface Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the deck height measurements in the Head Deck Surface section of Procedure 001-026 (Cylinder Block) in Section 1 of the QSK45 and QSK60 Series Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p>","tsb103825":"<h2>Cylinder Block Service Tools Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds a new service tool, Part Number 4919357, to Procedure 022-001 (Service Tools). This new tool is used to remove main bearings caps.</p>","tsb103847":"<h2>New Lubricating Oil Cooler Mounting Stud Gasket</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a new lubricating oil cooler mounting stud gasket for Industrial and Power Generator QSK45, QSK60, and QSK78 engines.</p><p>This is a product improvement and not subject to campaign.</p><p>The new gasket is an edge-molded gasket which has improved sealing capability.</p><p>The new oil cooler stud gasket, Part Number 3637730, replaces the oil cooler stud gasket, Part Number 3630969, on <b>all</b> QSK45, QSK60, and QSK78 engines. <b>Only</b> use a new oil cooler stud gasket, Part Number 3637730, for repairs.</p><p>The old oil cooler stud gasket, Part Number 3630969, is a paper gasket. The new gasket is an edge-molded gasket.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Procedure 007-045 (Lubricating Oil Cooler Cover) is being revised using three separate Service/Parts Topics to include the use of Loctite™ 271, Part Number 3375068, on oil cooler stud threads due to the introduction of the edge-molded gasket. The following bulletins are affected:</p></div></div><ul><li>QSK78 Series Engines Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 3666727</li><li>Industrial QSK45G and QSK60G Series Engines Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 4021383</li><li>QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</li></ul><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/07601238.png\" alt=\"07601238.png\"></figure><p>Old Paper Oil Cooler Stud Gasket, Part Number 3630969 (left) and New Edge-mounted Oil Cooler Stud Gasket, Part Number 3637730 (right)</p><p>During installation, use Loctite™ 271, Part Number 3375968, sparingly on the oil cooler stud threads.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Oil Cooler Stud Gasket</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Engine</td><td>Old Part Number</td><td>New Part Number</td><td>Part</td></tr><tr><td>QSK45, QSK60, QSK78</td><td>3630969</td><td>3637730</td><td>Gasket, Oil Cooler Stud</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Production Dates and Engine Serial Number First</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Engine</td><td>Production Dates</td><td>Engine Serial Number First</td></tr><tr><td>QSK45 QSK60 QSK78</td><td>30 January 2009 29 January 2009 12 November 2008</td><td>33176552 33177413 66301173</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","tsb103848":"<h2>New IMO Fuel Pump and Kits</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and is <b>not</b> subject to campaign or temporary repair practice (TRP).</p></div></div><p>This Service/Parts Topic describes an issue with the 2004 release of the IMO fuel pump for the following engines:</p><ul><li>QSK23 Industrial and Power Gen</li><li>QSK45 Industrial and Power Gen</li><li>QSK60 Industrial, Power Gen, and Marine</li><li>QSK78 Industrial and Power Gen.</li></ul><p>When the new fuel pump was released the old part numbers for the pumps were <b>not</b> correctly obsoleted. This Service/Parts Topic informs the field that the old part numbers are obsolete and should no longer be ordered.</p><p>The new IMO fuel pump that was released has a design change that places the weep hole in a different location. The location is dependant on both the type of engine and the application. Reference Table 1 for more information:</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Part Number Changes</th><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Part Name</td><td>Old Part Number</td><td>New Part Number</td><td>Engine Family</td></tr><tr><td>Pump, Fuel</td><td>4062157</td><td>4903531</td><td>QSK23</td></tr><tr><td>Pump, Fuel</td><td>4062157</td><td>4603530</td><td>QSK45</td></tr><tr><td>Pump, Fuel</td><td>4062156</td><td>4903532</td><td>QSK60</td></tr><tr><td>Pump, Fuel</td><td>4062155</td><td>4903533</td><td>Not Used</td></tr><tr><td>Pump, Fuel</td><td>4061675</td><td>4903534</td><td>QSK78</td></tr><tr><td>Kit, Housing Parts</td><td>4087914</td><td>4903561</td><td>QSK23</td></tr><tr><td>Kit, Housing Parts</td><td>4087914</td><td>4903562</td><td>QSK45</td></tr><tr><td>Kit, Housing Parts</td><td>4076762</td><td>4903563</td><td>QSK60</td></tr><tr><td>Kit, Housing Parts</td><td>4076761</td><td>4903564</td><td>Not Used</td></tr><tr><td>Kit, Housing Parts</td><td>4076760</td><td>4903565</td><td>QSK78</td></tr><tr><td>Kit, Housing Parts</td><td>4087971</td><td>4903566</td><td>QSK23</td></tr><tr><td>Kit, Front Cover Parts</td><td>4087971</td><td>4903567</td><td>QSK45, QSK60, and QSK78</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The weep hole relocation eliminates the low levels of external weep hole leakage by increasing the weep hole reservoir volume and increasing the evaporation rate by facing the weep hole toward the block. The weep hole moves from the 6 o&#x27;clock to the 9 o&#x27;clock position on the bottom of the fuel pump.</p>","tsb103850":"<h2>Lubricating Oil Cooler Cover Procedure, Install Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Install section of Procedure 007-045 (Lubricating Oil Cooler Cover) in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>, to include the use of Loctite™ 271, Part Number 3375068, on the oil cooler stud threads on the oil cooler cover. This change is due to the introduction of the edge-molded oil cooler stud gasket.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>The new lubricating oil cooler mounting stud gasket is being introduced with a separate Service/Parts Topic. Also, Procedure 007-045 (Lubricating Oil Cooler Cover) in the following bulletins is being revised using two separate Service/Parts Topics:</p></div></div><ul><li>QSK78 Series Engines Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 3666727</li><li>Industrial QSK45G and QSK60G Series Engines Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Bulletin 4021383.</li></ul>","tsb103852":"<h2>(Bearings, Connecting Rod) Procedure, Connecting Rod Bearing Thickness Specification Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Clean and Inspect for Reuse section of Procedure 001-005 (Bearings, Connecting Rod) to reflect the different connecting rod bearing thickness specifications for the new and old bearings.</p>","tsb103917":"<h2>Engine Lifting Brackets Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 016-001 (Engine Lifting Brackets) in Section 16 of QSK45 and QSK60 Series Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p><p>New capscrews are required after each removal of the engine lifting brackets.</p>","tsb103920":"<h2>Cylinder Head Procedure, Assemble Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Assemble section of Procedure 002-004 (Cylinder Head). The valve guide installation service tool part numbers have been added.</p>","tsb103922":"<h2>Eliminator™ Filter Procedure, Remove and Install Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 007-067 (Eliminator™ Filter) in Section 7 of the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. The changes to the Remove and Install sections are the result of a design change to the Eliminator™ filter mounting bracket.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>This is a product improvement and <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p></div></div>","tsb103923":"<h2>Fuel Filter Head Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Disassemble and Assemble Sections of Procedure 006-017 (Fuel Filter Head) in Section 6 of the QSK45 and QSK60 Series Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p><p>Removal specifications and torque specifications for the fuel filter head adapter spuds and adapter rings have been added.</p>","tsb103935":"<h2>(Fan Hub, Belt Driven) Procedure, Inspect for Reuse and Assemble Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the Inspect for Reuse and Assemble sections of Procedure 008-036 (Fan Hub, Belt Driven). The revisions include addition of the fan hub end clearance specification and information reflective to lubrication of the fan hub (if applicable).</p><p>This is a product improvement and <b>not</b> subject to campaign.</p>","tsb103946":"<h2>Connecting Rod Reuse Guidelines at Rebuild or Repair</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic supercedes Service/Parts Topic 06T1-34. Replace Service/Parts Topic 06T1-34 with this Topic.</p><p>This Service/Parts Topic informs the field that angle split connecting rods installed in QSK45/60 engines in fracturing rigs, excavators, loader, and mechanically driven haul trucks <b>must not</b> be reused at rebuild or repair, regardless of hours. Angle split connecting rods installed in QSK45/60 engines in electrically driven haul trucks, power generation, marine or other applications <b>must only</b> be reused at rebuild or repair if the connecting rods have less than 10,000 hours and pass the reuse guidelines.</p><p>Straight split connecting rods from any application can be reused regardless of the hours, provided they pass the reuse guidelines.</p><p>Warranty Impact</p><p>Warranty will not cover connecting rod malfunctions in which the connecting rods were not replaced during previous rebuild or repair, as directed by this Service/Parts Topic. Warranty will also follow the directions outlined in this Service/Parts Topic during the adjudication of warranty claims and when giving repair direction. This Service/Parts Topic does not authorize campaign or TRP actions.</p><p>Parts Information</p><p>The connecting rods should be replaced with new or ReCon® &quot;NX&quot; connecting rods when needed. This is a product improvement and is not subject to campaign.</p><p>Repair Procedure</p><p>Angle split connecting rods from QSK45/60 engines in fracturing rigs, excavators, loader, and mechanically driven haul trucks should <b>not</b> be reused at rebuild or repair, regardless of hours. Angle split connecting rods from QSK45/60 engines in electrically driven haul trucks, power generation, marine or other applications should only be reused at rebuild or repair if the connecting rods have less than 10,000 hours on them. If the connecting rod does <b>not</b> pass the reuse guidelines, it <b>mustnot</b> be reused, regardless of hours.</p><p>Straight split connecting rods from any application can be reused at rebuild or repair, regardless of hours, provided they pass reuse guidelines.</p><div class=\"callout note\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">i</span>Note · Примечание</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>Angle split and straight split connecting rods <b>can not</b> be mixed within an engine. All connecting rods must be the same design. Straight split connecting rods can <b>not</b> be installed into engines built prior to Engine Serial Number (ESN) 33172060, unless they have had a cylinder block upgrade.</p></div></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01600450.png\" alt=\"01600450.png\"></figure><p>This illustration shows the difference between a straight split connecting rod (1) and an angle split connecting rod (2).</p>","tsb103962":"<h2>Lubricating Oil Pump Procedure, Multiple Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This service/Parts Topic introduces multiple revisions to Procedure 007-031 (Lubricating Oil Pump) in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p><p>A Machine section has been added to the procedure. This new section shows a process for reworking the old lubricating oil pumps, Part Numbers 4100710 and 3638986 for the QSK45 engines and Part Numbers 3638987 and 4100711 for the QSK60 engines, to provide a clean oil supply to the lubricating oil pump idler bushing.</p>","tsb103980":"<h2>New Alternator and Accessory Drive Seal</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic replaces Service/Parts Topic 01T9-4. Replace Service/Parts Topic 01T9-4 with this Topic.</p><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces new accessory and alternator drive seal and pulleys for the QSK45 and QSK60 engines. The new accessory and alternator drive seal, Part Number 4080404, replaces the old accessory drive seal, Part Number 3171909. The new accessory drive seal will be included in Service Kit, Part Number 4085931. The service kit contains the items listed in Table 1.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 1, Service Kit, Part Number 4085931, Contents</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>4080404</td><td>Seal, Accessory Drive</td></tr><tr><td>4080395</td><td>Washer</td></tr><tr><td>4085923</td><td>Spacer, Mounting</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The new accessory and alternator drive seal is <b>not</b> a direct replacement for the old accessory and alternator drive seal. As a result, modification of the old pulley or installation of a new pulley is required. Refer to Table 2, Accessory and Alternator Drive Seal Matrix, below.</p><p>Accessory and Alternator Drive Seal Service Procedure Matrix</p><p>If replacing the accessory and alternator drive seal, Part Number 4080404, the seal is a direct replacement. For installation instructions, use the Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, QSK45 and QSK60 Engines, Bulletin 3666261.</p><p>If replacing the old accessory and alternator drive seal, Part Number 3171909, the following information applies. Refer to Table 2 for the correct procedure.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 2, Accessory and Alternator Drive Seal Matrix</th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pulley Part Number</td><td>Factory Option Part Number</td><td>Associated Procedure</td></tr><tr><td>3171728</td><td>PU6704</td><td>Alternator Drive Seal Procedure 001-001</td></tr><tr><td>3332188</td><td>PU6701</td><td>Alternator Drive Seal Procedure 001-001</td></tr><tr><td>3332203</td><td>PU6703</td><td>Alternator Drive Seal Procedure 001-001</td></tr><tr><td>4001382</td><td>PU6705</td><td>Alternator Drive Seal Procedure 001-001</td></tr><tr><td>4017444</td><td>AD6020</td><td>Accessory Drive Seal Procedure 001-003</td></tr><tr><td>4017445</td><td>AD6022</td><td>Accessory Drive Seal Procedure 001-003</td></tr><tr><td>4017446</td><td>AD6019</td><td>Accessory Drive Seal Procedure 001-003</td></tr><tr><td>4017447</td><td>AD6021</td><td>Accessory Drive Seal Procedure 001-003</td></tr><tr><td>4017448</td><td>AD6023</td><td>Accessory Drive Seal Procedure 001-003</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/09600116.png\" alt=\"09600116.png\"></figure><p>Alternator Drive Seal, Right Bank</p><p>Remove the alternator drive pulley and perform one of the following:</p><ol><li>Machine 2.1 mm [0.08 in] From the length A of the pulley or</li><li>Purchase a new pulley. See Table 3 for the correct new pulley part number.</li></ol><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 3, Alternator Drive Pulley Part Numbers, Right Bank</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Old Drive Pulley Part Number</td><td>New Drive Pulley Part Number</td></tr><tr><td>3171728</td><td>4080396</td></tr><tr><td>3332188</td><td>4080397</td></tr><tr><td>3332203</td><td>4080398</td></tr><tr><td>4001382</td><td>4080399</td></tr></tbody></table></div><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/09600117.png\" alt=\"09600117.png\"></figure><p>Accessory Drive Seal, Left Bank</p><p>Remove the accessory drive pulley and perform one of the following:</p><ul><li>Reuse the old pulley by installing the spacer, to increase the distance (B), provided in the seal service kit or</li><li>Purchase a new pulley. See Table 4 for the correct new pulley part number.</li></ul><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th>Table 4, Accessory Drive Pulley Part Numbers, Left Bank</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Old Drive Pulley Part Number</td><td>New Drive Pulley Part Number</td></tr><tr><td>4017444</td><td>4080400</td></tr><tr><td>4017445</td><td>4080401</td></tr><tr><td>4017446</td><td>4080425</td></tr><tr><td>4017447</td><td>4080402</td></tr><tr><td>4017448</td><td>4080403</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","tsb103984":"<h2>Lubricating Oil Filter Head Procedure, Assemble Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 007-015 (Lubricating Oil Filter Head) for the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. The adapter installation instructions have been revised.</p>","tsb103987":"<h2>Piston and Cylinder Liner Procedure, Install Section Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts topic introduces a revision to Procedure 001-045 (Piston and Cylinder Liner) in Section 1 of the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p><p>Proper connecting rod capscrew and bearing lubrication requirements have been added to the Install section of the procedure.</p>","tsb103988":"<h2>Piston and Connecting Rod Assembly Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 001-054 in Section 1 of the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>.</p><p>Information has been added to indicate this procedure is for angle split connecting rods only.</p><p>Information has also been added to specify the lubricant used on the bearings and connecting rod capscrews.</p>","tsb103998":"<h2>Multiple Group 10 Procedures, Caution Additions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic adds a Caution statement to Procedure 010-041 (Turbocharger Coolant Hoses), Procedure 010-045 (Turbocharger Oil Drain Line), and Procedure 010-046 (Turbocharger Oil Supply Line). The statement is below:</p><div class=\"callout warning\"><div class=\"callout-head\"><span class=\"callout-ico\">⚠</span>CAUTION · Осторожно</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p>When installing flexible hoses be sure that all the original clips are fitted and that the hoses do not contact any other hoses or engine components. Interference between hoses and other engine components can lead to leakages and engine damage.</p></div></div>","tsb104011":"<h2>Symptom Tree t105 (Lubricating Oil Pressure Low), Cause and Correction Step Addition</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises troubleshooting symptom tree t105 (Lubricating Oil Pressure Low) in Service Manual, QSK45 and QSK60, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. The order of inspection has been revised to aid in troubleshooting. An additional Cause and Correction step has been added to check malfunctioning sensors in the common sensor voltage supply circuit.</p>","tsb104033":"<h2>(Bearing, Main), Crankshaft, and Cylinder Block Procedure Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises the following procedures 001-006 (Bearing, Main), 001-016 (Crankshaft), and 001-026 (Cylinder Block) in Section 1 for the following publications:</p><ul><li>Service Manual, QSK45 and QSK60, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a></li><li>Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, Industrial QSK45 and QSK60G Series Engines, Bulletin 4021383</li><li>Troubleshooting and Repair Manual, QSK60G Generator CM700, Bulletin 4021396.</li></ul><p>The procedures include information for the removal and installation of the QSK60 fully counterweighted crankshaft.</p>","tsb104036":"<h2>Pre-Lubricating Oil Pump Procedure, Major Revision</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 007-063 (Pre-Lubricating Oil Pump) adding information about the &quot;Compact&quot; Prelub™ Pump and the &quot;High Volume&quot; Prelub™ Pump. This major revision affects all sections of this procedure.</p>","tsb104184":"<h2>Revision to Engine Installation Procedure</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic revises Procedure 000-002 (Engine Installation) in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>. Instructions to recheck the crankshaft endfloat have been added.</p>","tsb104222":"<h2>Fan Drive Idler Arm Assembly Procedure, Multiple Section Revisions</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This Service/Parts Topic introduces a revision to Procedure 008-029 (Fan Drive Idler Arm Assembly) in the QSK45 and QSK60 Service Manual, Bulletin Number <a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a> and the QSK78 Service Manual, Bulletin 3666727.</p><ul><li>The Clean and Inspect for Reuse section (<a class=\"lnk man\" href=\"#/manual/4021530\">4021530</a>) and Inspect for Reuse section (3666727) were modified to clarify the dimensions of the different types of shafts used.</li><li>The Assemble section was modified to include details on greasing the bearings on the slide arm type adjuster.</li></ul>","tsb110029":"<h2>QSKV Camshaft Stock Inspection</h2><h3>Warranty Statement</h3><p>The information in this document has no effect on present warranty coverage or repair practices, nor does it authorize TRP or Campaign actions.</p><h3>Contents</h3><p>This document instructs customers with stock camshafts in stock for the QSK45, QSK60, QSK60 Gas, and QSK78 engines, to perform a date code inspection on the camshaft.</p><p>To support an ongoing investigation, customers with the following camshaft part numbers in stock are requested to check the date code.</p><p>Part Numbers Affected:</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th><b>Camshaft Part Number</b></th><th><b>Engine Platform</b></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3411289</td><td>QSK60</td></tr><tr><td>3411290</td><td>QSK60</td></tr><tr><td>4017569</td><td>QSK60</td></tr><tr><td>4017570</td><td>QSK60</td></tr><tr><td>4001269</td><td>QSK60</td></tr><tr><td>4001270</td><td>QSK60</td></tr><tr><td>4006950</td><td>QSK78</td></tr><tr><td>4006951</td><td>QSK78</td></tr><tr><td>4001263</td><td>QSK45</td></tr><tr><td>4001264</td><td>QSK45</td></tr><tr><td>4001435</td><td>QSK45</td></tr><tr><td>4001436</td><td>QSK45</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h4>Suspect Dates:</h4><ul><li>Parts produced prior to 10-November-2010.</li></ul><h4>Description of Problem:</h4><ul><li>Some QSKV45/60/78 camshafts produced prior to 10-November-2010 are potentially at risk from a known quality issue</li><li>Atlas-produced camshafts are <b>not</b> affected.</li></ul><p>As per the instructions below, all QSKV45/60/78 camshafts in stock need to be checked. If the camshaft was produced after the 10-November-2010 or was manufactured by Atlas (USA) the camshaft is known to be good and can used. Below are details on identifying the camshaft manufacturer and date codes</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01k00005.png\" alt=\"01k00005.png\"></figure><p>If the camshaft is stamped with the initials ATS and USA, no further action is required.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01k00006.png\" alt=\"01k00006.png\"></figure><p>If the camshaft has been stamped with the initials EPCGE it is at risk and will need inspection.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01k00007.png\" alt=\"01k00007.png\"></figure><p>If the date code on an EPCGE camshaft is prior 10L0##, the camshaft was built prior to 10-November-2010, then contact the point of purchase and arrange for a return of the camshaft via a RGA (return goods authorization). The parts distribution center (PDC) will return parts to the supplier. The above illustration outlines the details on how the part date code is constructed and read.</p><figure class=\"fig\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/figures/01k00008.png\" alt=\"01k00008.png\"></figure><p>The illustration above is an example of a camshaft that was produced on 03M9 = 3-December-2009.</p><p>Produced before 10-November-2010 and therefore classified as &quot;At Risk&quot;.</p><p>For example, all of the camshafts in the following table would be classified as &quot;At Risk&quot;.</p><div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"doc-table\"><thead><tr><th><b>Date Code</b></th><th><b>Status</b></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>XX A 9</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX B 9</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX C 9</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX D 9</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX E 9</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX F 9</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX G 9</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX H 9</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX J 9</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX K 9</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX L 9</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX M 9</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX A 0</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX B 0</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX C 0</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX D 0</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX E 0</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX F 0</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX H 0</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX J 0</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX K 0</td><td>At Risk</td></tr><tr><td>XX L 0</td><td>At Risk</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>Document History</h3>"};
